[statement]
Observed: an earlier choice whose `!` entry forbids, through a name it
provides, the one candidate of a later name gives way. `top` needs `b`
and `c`; `b` 3, the best candidate for `b`, forbids `v`, which `c` 1, the
one candidate for `c`, provides. apk takes `b` 2. Contrast
`a-candidate-forbidding-an-installed-package-is-not-passed-over`, where
the `!` entry names the package itself.

[repository]
P:top
V:1
D:b c

P:c
V:1
p:v

P:b
V:3
D:!v

P:b
V:2

[request]
top

[answer apk-tools 3.0.9-r0]
install b 2
install c 1
install top 1
